  "title": "EU Countries Announce Migrant Deportation Hub in Rwanda",
  "summary": "Five EU countries, including Germany, Austria, the Netherlands, Denmark, and Greece, have announced plans to set up a'return hub' for rejected asylum seekers in Rwanda. This initiative is part of a pilot program that faces criticism for its potential human rights concerns.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Five EU countries (Germany, Austria, Netherlands, Denmark, Greece) announced plans to establish a'return hub' for rejected asylum seekers in Rwanda.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The program is based on the EU's newly agreed return law, allowing individuals who have exhausted their appeals to be sent to a third country.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The initiative has faced criticism for its potential moral failure, as highlighted by aid, trade union, and rights groups.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
