      "title": "Five EU states announce plans for immigration ‘return hubs’ in Rwanda",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/eu-states-immigration-return-hubs-rwanda",
      "description": "<p>Germany, Austria, Netherlands, Denmark and Greece likely to face challenges to policy criticised as ‘grave moral failing’</p><p>Five EU member states have announced plans to set up an offshore centre in Rwanda for people with no legal right to stay in Europe, in a pilot scheme that is expected to face legal challenges and has been denounced as “a grave moral failing”.</p><p>The five countries – Germany, Austria, the Netherlands, Denmark and Greece – are the first to seek to use the EU’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/26/meps-back-plans-for-return-hubs-raising-fears-of-human-rights-black-holes\">newly agreed returns law</a> that allows<em> </em>people who have exhausted all avenues of appeal against their removal from Europe to be sent to a third country.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/eu-states-immigration-return-hubs-rwanda\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
